<h2><strong>Book Before the School Year Starts</strong></h2>
<p>Timing matters here. The best time to schedule a children&#8217;s eye exam before school is about 6 to 8 weeks before the first day. That gives enough time for follow-up appointments if needed, for glasses to be made (we typically turn glasses around in 5–7 business days), and for your child to adjust to wearing them before they&#8217;re sitting in a classroom all day.</p>
<p>Waiting until the school year is already underway means your child has already been struggling for weeks.</p>
